POCKETSMART AI

Your Smart Budget & Recommendation Assistant

Phase 4: Project Planning

1. Project Goal

The goal of PocketSmart AI is to develop a simple budgeting and recommendation assistant that helps users record their income and expenses, analyze their spending, and receive useful budget recommendations.

2. Major Project Tasks

The project will be completed through the following tasks:

1. Finalize project requirements.
2. Design the system structure.
3. Design the user interface.
4. Set up the development environment.
5. Develop the main modules.
6. Implement income and expense calculations.
7. Implement budget and spending analysis.
8. Implement the recommendation feature.
9. Test the complete system.
10. Prepare project documentation.
11. Upload project files to GitHub.
12. Record the project demonstration video.

3. Suggested Timeline

Stage| Work
Day 1| Requirement analysis and project planning
Day 2| System and UI design
Day 3–4| Basic project development
Day 5–6| Income, expense and budget modules
Day 7| Spending analysis and recommendations
Day 8| Testing and error correction
Day 9| Documentation
Day 10| GitHub upload and organization
Final Day| Demo video and final verification

4. Team Planning

If the project is completed as a team, the work can be divided into:

- Member 1: Project planning and documentation
- Member 2: User interface/design
- Member 3: Backend and data processing
- Member 4: AI/recommendation and testing
- Member 5: Integration and demonstration

The exact division can be changed according to the number of team members.

5. Project Resources

The following resources will be required:

- Project Document
- Project Reference Video
- Development environment
- Required programming tools
- Database, if required
- AI/ML tools or libraries, if required
- GitHub repository
- Google Drive for demonstration video

6. Risk Management

Possible project risks include:

- Delay in receiving project requirements.
- Technical errors during development.
- Difficulty integrating different modules.
- Insufficient testing time.
- Problems uploading files or demo videos.

7. Risk Solutions

To reduce these risks:

- Review the official project requirements before development.
- Complete the project module by module.
- Test each feature after development.
- Keep backup copies of project files.
- Upload files to GitHub regularly.
- Complete the demonstration video before the final deadline.

8. Final Deliverables

The planned final deliverables are:

1. Working PocketSmart AI project.
2. Public GitHub repository.
3. Project documentation.
4. Project demonstration video.
5. Phase-wise project records.

Note

This planning schedule is a proposed plan. The actual development schedule should be adjusted according to the official SmartBridge Project Document, Reference Video, team size, and required technology.
